 :reads
 {:known-defect-list {:source "Open findings in the last run's report, review notes and Lean or certificate mismatches" :kind :read}
  :known-defects-cleared {:source "Commits or agent reports saying the listed defects were fixed; an agent's report stands in for checking each one" :kind :proxy}
  :counted-run-under-way {:source "Operator's click authorisation and the run or click ledger" :kind :read}
  :run-reached-its-end {:source "Terminal status of the click or pipeline run" :kind :read}
  :gap-between-claim-and-run {:source "An operator turn questioning the run, standing in for a direct comparison of report and run trace" :kind :proxy}
  :written-class-level-plan {:source "The E- excursion file, audit or set of work packets named in the turn" :kind :read}
  :verdict-from-independent-authority {:source "Lean run-time certificate output or the cold comparator result" :kind :read}}
 :rationale "Joe keeps driving an expensive machine through the same loop: he refuses to pay for another run while known defects are open, then authorises a run of a stated size. When the run fails partway, he wants the failure repaired in place so the run finishes. Once it finishes, he does not take the report at its word; he asks what actually happened, and any gap gets widened into a written investigation of the whole class of problem. The result is then tied to Lean or the comparator, because agents' claims of success have repeatedly been wrong. In one session the order closes on itself, with the fix put under the certificates and more clicks then authorised to test them, but that return to the second step appears only there and so is not recorded as an edge."
